Fix the FAT volume-label comparison width in UniXNU's RamDiskDxe

Applies to UniXNU/package/UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.c
and UniXNU/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c.

EspAt() identifies the payload volume by comparing the FAT BPB label field:

    return (CompareMem (Bpb + 0x47, ESP_LABEL, 8) == 0) ||
           (CompareMem (Bpb + 0x36, ESP_LABEL, 8) == 0);

The BPB label is an 8-byte, space-padded field, and CompareMem always reads 8
bytes, so ESP_LABEL has to be exactly 8 characters with no terminator inside
that window. The board was ported from a tree where the label was DADA2ESP -
eight characters, which happened to satisfy the constraint. Renaming the
volume to MIROESP leaves a 7-character literal, so the 8th byte compared is
the string's NUL terminator while the BPB holds a space. The comparison can
never match, the driver publishes no volume, the menu falls back to its
built-in configuration (four action entries, no kernel), and the phone powers
off for lack of an OS.

Symptom on screen, before the fix:

    built-in . v9 h5CC5000 t1 f0 iD5EC6000+21322000 pB0070000
    drivers 0 loaded / 0 failed   kits 0

f0 is the FAT verdict (no volume found). After the fix the same boot reaches
the kernel and its framebuffer.

The same commit restores the built-in menu timeout, which an earlier debugging
session had raised to 600 s. With no payload the menu then sits for ten
minutes instead of ten seconds, which reads as a hang.

diff --git a/package/UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.c b/package/UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.c
--- a/package/UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.c
+++ b/package/UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.c
@@ -436,7 +436,10 @@
 #define KERNEL_WINDOW_SIZE   0x10000000ULL
 #define ESP_SCAN_STEP        0x1000ULL
-#define ESP_LABEL            "MIROESP"
+// The FAT BPB volume label is an 8-byte space-padded field, so the literal
+// must be exactly 8 bytes: a shorter string adds a NUL that never matches.
+#define ESP_LABEL            "MIROESP "
 
 STATIC
 UINT64
@@ -470,6 +473,7 @@
 
   Bpb = (CONST UINT8 *)(UINTN)Start;
+  STATIC_ASSERT (sizeof (ESP_LABEL) - 1 == 8, "the label must fill the 8-byte BPB field");
   return (CompareMem (Bpb + 0x47, ESP_LABEL, 8) == 0) ||
          (CompareMem (Bpb + 0x36, ESP_LABEL, 8) == 0);
 }
diff --git a/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c b/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c
--- a/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c
+++ b/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 STATIC CONST CHAR8  mBuiltinConfig[] =
   "version = 1\n"
   "[boot]\n"
-  "timeout = 600\n"
+  "timeout = 10\n"
   "rotate = 2\n"
   "[ui]\n"
   "title = \"UniXNU\"\n"
